{
  "title": "iOS Settings has no ingredient recognition panel",
  "description": "Web Settings (ramekin-ui/src/pages/SettingsPage.tsx) has an 'Ingredient recognition' section backed by GET /api/ingredient-names/status: recognized/estimated/not food/unknown/pending/failed counts, the failed names with their errors, and a 'Retry failed' button (POST /api/ingredient-names/retry). iOS Settings has no counterpart, so failed names can only be seen and retried from the web. \
Either add the same section to iOS Settings (poll every 2 s while names are pending; on a failed status request show the section as unavailable and retry with backoff, as web does) or decide the panel is web-only and record that. \
Phases of the calorie redesign (doc/calorie-estimates.md) may change which states exist; check before building.",
